# deploy/docker/crontab.tmpl — the template render-crontab.sh renders over
# deploy/docker/crontab at every container start (design decision D5). The
# at-sign placeholders below come from config.json's `schedule`: several
# active nodes on one shared Claude account must not all fire at once, so
# each node lands on its own minute for the two heavy pipelines — a stable
# hash of NODE_NAME by default, CYCLE_MINUTE in .env to choose, drawn only
# from the minutes schedule.excluded_minutes does not rule out.
#
# 38,53 is a comma-separated minute list, not a single minute
# (issue #248, "faster heartbeat"): the node's own minute, then every
# schedule.cycle_interval_minutes after it within the hour, each occurrence
# dropped if it lands on an excluded minute. cron's minute field accepts
# such a list natively. cycle_interval_minutes=60 collapses this back to
# the single-minute, once-per-hour shape every release before it carried.
# An idle firing stays cheap: lib/noop-skip.sh short-circuits before the
# Co-Ordinator runs when nothing a fingerprint covers has changed.
#
# 22 is schedule.doctor_offset_minutes past the node's own base
# minute (mod 60), the same jitter the review line above uses — one node's hourly
# `doctor.sh --unattended` pass (agent-ops#543) lands away from every other
# node's, and away from this node's own heavy pipelines. `doctor.sh` exits
# non-zero on a `fail` verdict, which here is routine — a misconfigured
# `Priority` field found once an hour, not a broken job — so the line ends
# `|| true`: nothing on this image reads a cron job's exit status (no
# MAILTO, no healthcheck), but a future reader of `docker compose logs`
# must not mistake supercronic's own "job failed" line for a crashed
# script. The run's actual verdict travels through the file it writes
# (state_dir/.doctor-status.json) to the dashboard, not through this exit
# status.
#
# 29 2 is schedule.revert_rate_offset_minutes
# past the node's own base minute (mod 60), the same jitter the doctor line
# above uses, but daily rather than hourly — one node's own
# `scripts/publish-revert-rate.sh` pass (agent-ops#579) runs the merged-PR
# miner over a bounded window and appends this repository's rolling-window,
# cumulative-since-baseline and stored-baseline revert-or-follow-up rates to
# `revert-rate.jsonl`, replicated fleet-wide like `log.jsonl` (never rotated,
# never excluded from the state branch). It ends `|| true` for the identical
# reason the doctor line does: nothing on this image reads a cron job's exit
# status, and a routine `not-met` reading against the stored baseline is not a
# crashed script.
#
# 15 4 is schedule.tech_debt_archive_offset_minutes
# past the node's own base minute (mod 60), the same jitter shape the
# revert-rate line above uses, daily rather than hourly — one node's own
# `scripts/publish-tech-debt-archive.sh` pass (agent-ops#878, D15 as revised)
# mirrors every `pw::type:tech-debt`-labelled issue, per configured
# repository, into the state repository's own git history, one JSON file per
# issue. It ends `|| true` for the same reason the revert-rate line does:
# nothing on this image reads a cron job's exit status, and a repository
# whose label search or archive write failed this run is simply retried on
# the next one, not a crashed script.
#
# Everything not a placeholder is documented in the baked crontab, which is
# also the fallback whenever this template cannot be rendered.

LOGDIR=/home/agent/.local/state/poetic-agents

*/5 * * * *  /app/scripts/publish-dashboard-launcher.sh
38,53 * * * *  /app/agent-cycle.sh  >> $LOGDIR/cron.log        2>&1
7 3 * * *  /app/review-cycle.sh >> $LOGDIR/review-cron.log 2>&1
22 * * * *  /app/scripts/doctor.sh --unattended >> $LOGDIR/doctor.log 2>&1 || true
29 2 * * *  /app/scripts/publish-revert-rate.sh >> $LOGDIR/revert-rate.log 2>&1 || true
15 4 * * *  /app/scripts/publish-tech-debt-archive.sh >> $LOGDIR/tech-debt-archive.log 2>&1 || true

*/5 * * * *  /app/scripts/state-sync.sh push  >> $LOGDIR/state-sync.log 2>&1
*/7 * * * *  /app/scripts/state-sync.sh fetch >> $LOGDIR/state-sync.log 2>&1

19 * * * *  /app/scripts/rotate-logs.sh >> $LOGDIR/dashboard.log 2>&1
